=== ip6tables-translate ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ip6tables-translate v1.8.10 (nf_tables)

Either long or short options are allowed.


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ip6tables-translate -[ACD] chain rule-specification [options]
  ip6tables-translate -I chain [rulenum] rule-specification [options]
  ip6tables-translate -R chain rulenum rule-specification [options]
  ip6tables-translate -D chain rulenum [options]
  ip6tables-translate -[LS] [chain [rulenum]] [options]
  ip6tables-translate -[FZ] [chain] [options]
  ip6tables-translate -[NX] chain
  ip6tables-translate -E old-chain-name new-chain-name
  ip6tables-translate -P chain target [options]
  ip6tables-translate -h (print this help information)


POSITIONALS (3) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  chain
  rule-specification
  rulenum


FLAGS (34) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-A, --append chain            Append to chain
-C, --check chain             Check for the existence of a rule
-D, --delete chain            Delete matching rule from chain
-D, --delete chain rulenum    Delete rule rulenum (1 = first) from chain
-I, --insert chain [rulenum]  Insert in chain as rulenum (default 1=first)
-R, --replace chain rulenum   Replace rule rulenum (1 = first) in chain
-L, --list [chain [rulenum]]  List the rules in a chain or all chains
-S, --list-rules [chain [rulenum]] Print the rules in a chain or all chains
-F, --flush [chain]           Delete all rules in chain or all chains
-Z, --zero [chain [rulenum]]  Zero counters in chain or all chains
-N, --new chain               Create a new user-defined chain
-X, --delete-chain [chain]    Delete a user-defined chain
-P, --policy chain target     Change policy on chain to target
-E, --rename-chain old-chain new-chain Change chain name, (moving any
                              references)
-4, --ipv4                    Error (line is ignored by ip6tables-restore)
-6, --ipv6                    Nothing (line is ignored by iptables-restore)
[!] -p, --protocol proto      protocol: by number or name, eg. `tcp'
[!] -s, --source address[/mask][...] source specification
[!] -d, --destination address[/mask][...] destination specification
[!] -i, --in-interface input name[+] network interface name ([+] for
                              wildcard)
-j, --jump target             target for rule (may load target extension)
-g, --goto chain              jump to chain with no return
-m, --match match             extended match (may load extension)
-n, --numeric                 numeric output of addresses and ports
[!] -o, --out-interface output name[+] network interface name ([+] for
                              wildcard)
-t, --table table             table to manipulate (default: `filter')
-v, --verbose                 verbose mode
-w, --wait [seconds]          maximum wait to acquire xtables lock before
                              give up
    --line-numbers            print line numbers when listing
-x, --exact                   expand numbers (display exact values)
    --modprobe=<command>      try to insert modules using this command
-c, --set-counters PKTS BYTES set the counter during insert/append
[!] -V, --version             print package version.
-h
